WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
A 9 billion parameter model now follows unseen legal procedures at 93-100% after one training run. This is Models &amp; Agents, Episode 204. FlowSpec, described in an archive paper, generated 2,506 conversations from 297 randomized procedures for a tie outbound call agent. The machine readable specification writes the instructions, gates the tools, supplies the supervision, and defines the tests. The agent may speak only from an

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:36.420
approved sentence catalog, documented checks had sat at 67 to 71 percent, while grounded

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:40.240
checks already passed at 97 to 100 percent before training.

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:47.600
Scenario pass rate moved from 15 to 43 to 40 to 43 across four held outflows, three

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:52.260
of them debt collection procedures from a withheld lineage, and one non debt procedure.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:57.960
An audit of the shared specification found 11 defects, three of which the metric missed,

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:02.880
and the small self-hosted policy transferred across creditor-specific revisions of the

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:07.040
same legal rules with no extra fine-tuning on the target procedures.

00:01:07.904 --> 00:01:14.324
Training from scratch on approximately 12 trillion tokens produced LLMJP4 as an 8 billion

00:01:14.324 --> 00:01:18.764
dense model and a 32 billion A3B mixture of experts model.

00:01:19.364 --> 00:01:24.404
Explicit criteria for data, external models, and software selection appear in an archive

00:01:24.404 --> 00:01:28.664
technical report and the full development process is released for independent

00:01:28.664 --> 00:01:33.664
verification and reproduction. The new models post substantial gains over prior

00:01:33.664 --> 00:01:38.644
LLM JP releases and stay competitive with open-weight systems at comparable

00:01:38.644 --> 00:01:45.204
parameter counts. Attention layers in Lama 3.2 YB instruct get replaced by Titan

00:01:45.204 --> 00:01:50.484
Lama's hierarchical memory, a retrofit documented on archive. Full fidelity

00:01:50.484 --> 00:01:56.224
attention stays on recent tokens, and history is compressed into recurrent fixed-size neural memory

00:01:56.224 --> 00:02:05.464
modules behind a block-wise attention mask. Accuracy on quality rises from 23.87% to 40.51%,

00:02:05.464 --> 00:02:16.004
and on long-health from 14.50% to 40.75%. Pre-fill runs more than 20% faster, and decode runs 37% faster

00:02:16.004 --> 00:02:20.804
at medium-context lengths, with 24% lower steady-state memory usage.

00:02:21.795 --> 00:02:26.835
The SWAP happens after the original pre-training, so no new model has to be trained from scratch.

00:02:27.415 --> 00:02:32.115
Copy-paste language models add a lightweight copy-paste head beside the standard language

00:02:32.115 --> 00:02:37.115
modeling head, creating an alternative gradient path that eases the language modeling head

00:02:37.115 --> 00:02:40.375
bottleneck, according to an archive NLP paper.

00:02:40.375 --> 00:02:46.555
models from 135 million to 1.7 billion parameters improve across scales and

00:02:46.555 --> 00:02:50.915
backbones with negligible training and inference overhead. The extra head

00:02:50.915 --> 00:02:55.015
supplies a direct gradient route that bypasses the primary language modeling

00:02:55.015 --> 00:03:00.315
head during back propagation. Check-span multiple scales and different backbone

00:03:00.315 --> 00:03:05.135
architectures with gains in training efficiency, downstream performance, and

00:03:05.135 --> 00:03:08.175
operating points in long-context and retrieval settings.

00:03:09.147 --> 00:03:15.787
Baby LM's 2026 multilingual track received QuenFant, a Quen3-based model trained on concise

00:03:15.787 --> 00:03:21.007
parallel text that an archive paper says was produced by summarization and translation.

00:03:21.747 --> 00:03:27.267
A character-level vocabulary and a larger model size both reached through low-rank adaptation

00:03:27.267 --> 00:03:31.047
or Lora adapters were required for full performance.

00:03:31.047 --> 00:03:35.287
At submission time, Quinn Fant ranked first in the multilingual track.

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:42.310
Hero learns reusable prompt updates from execution verified successes and failures, and validates

00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:45.330
revisions before adoption, per an archive report.

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:50.970
At test time, it treats generated code as an instant specific harness refined by execution

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:51.570
feedback.

00:03:52.050 --> 00:03:58.610
Across four text to SQL, text to cipher, a graph query language, and text to Python benchmarks,

00:03:58.610 --> 00:04:02.310
It improves pass at 1 by 7.6 points offline.

00:04:02.870 --> 00:04:05.730
Test time refinement adds another 2.0 points

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:07.690
and improves execution efficiency.

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:10.810
Prompt revisions are extracted only from cases

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:12.850
where execution confirms correctness

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:14.470
or exposes a clear failure.

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:17.490
And the generated program itself becomes the harness

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:19.350
for further execution-driven edits.

00:04:20.396 --> 00:04:23.196
User feedback gets decomposed into atomic rules

00:04:23.196 --> 00:04:25.996
by skill grain, which an archive paper says

00:04:25.996 --> 00:04:31.116
as predicts transferability and keeps only rules suited to future requests, using rubric

00:04:31.116 --> 00:04:36.776
guided rewards and fine-grained credit assignment. Across three base models on five personalized

00:04:36.776 --> 00:04:42.456
writing tasks, it posts the best overall average in both in-domain and out-of-domain settings.

00:04:43.056 --> 00:04:47.776
Each rule is scored for content quality and for the decision to retain or discard it.

00:04:48.376 --> 00:04:53.036
Reinforcement learning jointly optimizes skill induction and the skill condition generation

00:04:53.036 --> 00:05:00.589
step. Percy Valbench contains 403 multi-episode scenarios, testing nine controlled error subtypes

00:05:00.589 --> 00:05:06.429
across under, over, and misapplied state personalization. On the human-evaluated subset,

00:05:06.769 --> 00:05:14.129
the strongest-large language model, or LLM, evaluator recognizes 63.9% of under-personalization

00:05:14.129 --> 00:05:20.409
errors, while humans recognize 94.4%, according to the accompanying archive write-up.

00:05:20.409 --> 00:05:24.229
Highlighting relevant history raises recognition only slightly.

00:05:24.769 --> 00:05:30.769
Five LLM evaluators ran on the full set, human audits confirmed that generated errors match

00:05:30.769 --> 00:05:35.469
their intended types, and the largest gap sits on under-personalization cases.

00:05:36.109 --> 00:05:43.569
Napoli public-figured tweets feed any PCE, which keeps 3,189 sentences where two annotators

00:05:43.569 --> 00:05:47.469
agree on polarity, from 5,614 tweets.

00:05:47.469 --> 00:05:55.769
On the 3-class benchmark, NEP Burda reaches 0.877 macro F1, a balanced score across classes,

00:05:56.029 --> 00:06:03.249
and 3 commercial LLMs reach 0.882 to 0.8960 shot, as reported on archive.

00:06:03.869 --> 00:06:12.149
On the 5-point scale, Claude Opus 5.5 beats the best encoders by 0.10 to 0.12 macro F1.

00:06:12.149 --> 00:06:23.129
Put the non-spacing Devanigari Marks back and macro-F1 moves plus 0.084 or minus 0.095 depending on the tokenizer.

00:06:24.169 --> 00:06:29.489
766 five point sentences carry two adjacent labels that are both accepted during training.

00:06:30.325 --> 00:06:40.725
Topic Merge first oversegments documents into fine-grained microclusters, then runs an LLM guided iterative merge that uses local neighborhood context to consolidate topics.

00:06:40.725 --> 00:06:45.925
On the bills and wiki data sets, an archive evaluation says it reaches state-of-the-art

00:06:45.925 --> 00:06:52.245
clustering while cutting LLM calls by more than 92% versus methods that score whole documents.

00:06:52.785 --> 00:06:57.665
That first cut yields semantically pure microclusters with preliminary semantic labels.

00:06:58.285 --> 00:07:02.905
The merge stage then arbitrates candidate pairs with neighborhood contacts before any join

00:07:02.905 --> 00:07:03.685
is executed.

00:07:03.685 --> 00:07:11.185
Conventions centered on the United States make up 62.4% to 94.4% of matched signals across

00:07:11.185 --> 00:07:17.385
11 text benchmarks in an archive audit of 16 evaluation resources across seven dimensions.

00:07:18.005 --> 00:07:23.565
Geographic visibility in five image text resources correlates with national gross domestic product

00:07:23.565 --> 00:07:32.305
or GDP share, with a mean Pearson correlation of 0.780. All 16 resources operationalize source user

00:07:32.305 --> 00:07:35.985
context, but non-operationalized target user context.

00:07:36.465 --> 00:07:41.305
Pared scoring on drop and truthful QA shows how meaning-preserving answer variants move

00:07:41.305 --> 00:07:47.225
exact match and reference similarity scores, and the audit covers content, metadata, documentation,

00:07:47.705 --> 00:07:53.237
and scoring procedures. Generate synthetic procedures with the flow spec recipe on a regulated

00:07:53.237 --> 00:07:59.837
workflow you already run, then measure compliance lift on held out flows. Run the NEPC-3 class and

00:07:59.837 --> 00:08:05.237
five-point splits against a Napoli-capable model you already use, and watch how Devonigari

00:08:05.237 --> 00:08:12.437
Mark Restoration moves macro-F1. Swap the Titan Lama memory modules into a Lama 3.2-1B

00:08:12.437 --> 00:08:19.397
instruct checkpoint and score quality and long-health at 128K context. Score Perseval Benches

00:08:19.397 --> 00:08:24.677
multi-episode scenarios with your current LLM judge, and separate under-personalization

00:08:24.677 --> 00:08:26.717
errors from over-personalization errors.

00:08:27.794 --> 00:08:33.674
National labs are expected to ship more sovereign LLMs that follow the LLMJP4 transparency model.

00:08:34.294 --> 00:08:38.654
Execution verified harness updates of the Hero Kind are slated to land in further

00:08:38.654 --> 00:08:39.494
agent frameworks.

00:08:40.174 --> 00:08:44.494
Additional base model families are likely to get post-training memory retrofits of their

00:08:44.494 --> 00:08:44.754
own.

00:08:45.314 --> 00:08:50.254
If you pop the hood on layer-ablation studies, the early versus late comparison runs across

00:08:50.254 --> 00:08:53.134
two corpora that do not share a target token mix.

00:08:53.134 --> 00:08:58.434
A blading early layers is scored against a blading late layers, then the damage is compared

00:08:58.434 --> 00:08:59.294
on each corpus.

00:08:59.914 --> 00:09:04.714
A bigger early layer hit on one corpus gets read as proof that the task lives at a special

00:09:04.714 --> 00:09:05.734
depth in the network.

00:09:06.374 --> 00:09:08.954
That reading is the marketing of depth specialization.

00:09:09.574 --> 00:09:13.954
The engineering comparison is actually performed over different target token distributions.

00:09:14.714 --> 00:09:19.034
Math solutions contain far more white space and numbers than encyclopedia pros.

00:09:19.034 --> 00:09:23.134
those extra white space and number tokens change which predictions the

00:09:23.134 --> 00:09:27.634
ablation is being scored on. Break the pooled interaction apart by target token

00:09:27.634 --> 00:09:31.854
type and the positive early versus late interaction appears only on white

00:09:31.854 --> 00:09:36.634
space tokens. Drop white space from the score and the pooled effect flip sign in

00:09:36.634 --> 00:09:41.194
every one of the three fully decomposed model instances. Match the full target

00:09:41.194 --> 00:09:45.554
mixture across the two corpora and that flip still appears in two of the three

00:09:45.554 --> 00:09:51.154
instances. A tokenizer only screen puts each held out pair into the risk region that the label

00:09:51.154 --> 00:09:57.214
already predicts. Position matching and adversarial reassignment of token types both leave the diagnosis

00:09:57.214 --> 00:10:03.234
in place. Look one token ahead and a smaller content word effect tracks how many content targets

00:10:03.234 --> 00:10:09.134
the untouched model already predicts. Use a depth specialization claim only after the target token

00:10:09.134 --> 00:10:15.074
mixture is reported. The effect is split by token type, and the sign still survives mixture matching.

00:10:15.734 --> 00:10:21.474
Skip those three checks, and the result is an artifact of the evaluation corpora rather than model architecture.

00:10:22.194 --> 00:10:28.794
Before we go, expanded low resource language benchmarks are being built to test transfer from high resource pre-training.

